Extracts every data-bearing AFID slot from an already-decrypted PPR-PFS image. Empty
-1 slots are preserved implicitly by gaps between the returned numeric assignments;
zero-length files are assigned automatically after the two FIDX boundary slots.

Case-insensitive path globs excluded from Kraken compression. Paths use forward slashes;
* matches within one component and ** crosses directory separators.
The default mirrors the reference image, where every file below sce_sys is raw.

member.param:
Optional staged outer-PFS file. When supplied, its bytes replace the PFS range in the CNT;
this avoids embedding the same multi-gigabyte image in a short-lived intermediate CNT.
The CNT may end exactly at its declared PFS offset, containing only metadata.

member.summary:
PS5 finalized-image and CNT digest algorithms. The one primitive is SHA3-256;
see the file header for the exact preimage of each digest and the boundary of what is and is
not reproducible off-console. All methods are managed (SHA-3, .NET 10).

Builds type-18 metadata for a file-backed mount image. This overload needs only the mount
length because publisher nwonly integrity mapping is derived from ;
it avoids retaining a multi-gigabyte FIH/PFS/CNT byte array.

The CNT (sce_sys) entry table for the <entries> section. When non-empty the table
is emitted exactly as the tool does (num attribute plus one <entry> per file);
when empty the section is omitted.

A finalized debug image (\x7FFIH, signed byte 0x00) — a full package, and the only
form installable on a PS5 with debug mode enabled. The structure and embedded CNT are exact;
the finalization digest table is debug-key gated and filled best-effort (see
). This is the default output.

A build-scoped LRU with reservations for unfinished work. Factories run outside the lock;
concurrent callers share their result, and never wait for the ordered output writer.
Charges include the caller's payload estimate and an allowance for entry/index overhead.
